# ==============================================================================
# .gitignore for the Basilisk repo.
#
# This header used to read ".dockerignore - Controls what gets sent to
# Docker build context / Intentionally mirrors .gitignore", copied in
# from skewed-emacs during the split.  It was never true here: basilisk
# builds no image -- no Dockerfile, no .dockerignore -- it orchestrates
# other people's.  In skewed-emacs the claim IS true, and structurally
# so: .dockerignore there is a tracked symlink to .gitignore.
#
# The practical consequence, and the reason this is worth a paragraph:
# a rule here answers to git ALONE.  Do not keep a line "for the docker
# build" -- see the .git/ note at the bottom.  Corrected 2026-08-16.
# ==============================================================================

# ==============================================================================
# Emacs temporary/backup files
# ==============================================================================
*~
.#*
**/#*#
*.elc

# ==============================================================================
# Log files
# ==============================================================================
*.log
*.log*

# ==============================================================================
# Emacs user directories (regenerated, user-specific)
# ==============================================================================
# ==============================================================================
.authinfo
.authinfo.gpg
.env
.tokens/
*token*

*-stack-compose.yml

# Development overlay files (local, not committed)

*-overlay.yml

*-dev-overlay.yml

# ==============================================================================
# Generated MCP configs
# ==============================================================================

mcp/*mcp*
!mcp/merge-mcp-configs.el
!mcp/mcp-*
# mcp.toml is TRACKED, like mcp-container.json and mcp-windows.json
# beside it -- but it is the one base config with no dash in its name,
# so `!mcp/mcp-*' above sails straight past it and `mcp/*mcp*' claims
# it.  That is the same tracked-and-ignored contradiction as the
# claude_desktop_config.json note below, sitting one regeneration away
# from biting: generate-configs.el writes mcp.toml into this directory
# whenever the BASE configs are generated (empty output prefix), and
# from that moment the clone is permanently dirty and `repos deploy'
# stops pulling basilisk on every host without saying so.  Found by
# audit 2026-08-16, before it fired.
!mcp/mcp.toml
# Written back into this clone by every `./basilisk up' (the merge output
# for Claude Desktop).  It was ALSO committed, and a tracked file ignores
# .gitignore entirely -- so every start left the clone dirty, and
# `repos deploy' then refused to pull basilisk on sally and shelly,
# silently, for as long as that lasted.  Untracked 2026-08-16; if it ever
# needs to be tracked again, it wants a .example suffix and a generated
# sibling, not a rule that cannot fire.
mcp/claude_desktop_config.json
mcp/opening-prompt-local.md

# The ship's minted name (generate-env.sh); per-clone, per-instance
# identity, like .env -- never another ship's business.
.ship
.ship-*

# ==============================================================================
# Per-host state, written by <host>-stack/install into THIS clone
# ==============================================================================
# host.env carries the image-variant pin for the machine this clone runs
# on.  Tracking it puts one ship's pin in every ship's repo: it arrived
# here saying EMACS_IMAGE_VARIANT=full from narad-stack/install, so a
# clone pinned to lite gets a heavy Captain back on the next pull.
systemd/host.env

# Host overlay yard output, copied in by <host>-stack/install and
# re-copied by every `./basilisk up'.  The UNPREFIXED
# generated/services-generated.el is the base file and stays tracked --
# it is the yard's own output and every ship needs it.  The <host>-stack-
# prefixed ones belong to whichever machine ran install last, and get
# rewritten under you on every start, so tracking them just strands one
# ship's roster in every ship's repo.
generated/*-stack-services-generated.el

# The overlay crew ledger and templated fittings, carried in by
# <host>-stack/install, plus the copies the yard rewrites from the
# ledger on every `./basilisk up': per-host state, same as host.env
# above.  The UNPREFIXED generated/crew.env is the base ship's own
# ledger and stays tracked.  History rhymed here: the first install
# flow copied the overlay ledger ONTO tracked generated/crew.env,
# and `repos deploy' stopped pulling basilisk on shelly, silently --
# the same failure this file already describes twice above
# (2026-08-17; see claude_desktop_config.json and the mcp.toml
# near-miss).  Installs never overwrite tracked files.
generated/*-crew.env
templates/
generated/cyclops.sexp
generated/*-services-init.cl

# ==============================================================================
# Build artifacts & caches
# ==============================================================================
# (.git/ was listed here and removed 2026-08-16: git never tracks its own
# directory, so the rule could only ever be noise.  It earns its place in
# a .dockerignore -- but this repo has none, and this file mirrors
# nothing, so there is no "keep it THERE" to point at.  It is simply
# gone.  See the header.)
tmp/

# ==============================================================================
# Art-direction working papers
# ==============================================================================
# Conversations with the painters.  They mix raw brainstorm with
# settled canon and are not written for the public books; what they
# establish is distilled into the canon scrolls (and the owner's own
# ledgers).  The images they produce graduate into artwork/ proper.
artwork/direction/

# The standing muster roll (muster_crew): the minted name of each
# room's keeper, per instance -- uncommitted like .ship above.
.muster
.muster-*
# The log of ships: every ship this galaxy raised and buried, name
# and dates -- some names go down famous.
.ships-log
# The slipway lock (one raise or stand-down at a time); .conn is its
# retired pre-2026-08-24 name, swept by the first take_the_slipway.
.slipway
.conn
